# HoovyTools - what never reaches the repository.
#
# THE CONVENTION, enforced here rather than remembered:
#     name      required. The add-on does not start without it.
#     _name     optional. Shipped, but the add-on runs if you delete it.
#     __name    development only. Never shipped.  <-- this file's job
#
# So a single rule covers it: anything whose name starts with two
# underscores, except the package marker itself.

__*/
!__init__.py

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.blend1

# Runtime state, not shipped content: the folders a USER added, with their
# absolute paths in them. `_config` follows the underscore convention (the
# add-on runs without it) but nothing in it belongs in the repository.
_config/

# Reports written at runtime. This folder is `_Logs` and NOT `__Logs` so that
# a user told "check the log" finds it where they look. That choice costs the
# automatic exclusion - `__*/` above does not reach one underscore - so this
# line is the only thing keeping every run's output out of the repository.
# Delete it and the logs start getting committed. See core/paths.py.
_Logs/

# `images/` is REQUIRED and IS shipped - it lost its underscore on
# 2026-08-24 because the panel is built around it and an install without
# it is a degraded install, not a normal one.

# 3.0.0: the QCs written from imported models (core/mdl_flex.py) - runtime output, rewritten by the next import.
_QC Face Data/_Generated/
*.qc.tmp

# Windows writes this when a folder gets a custom icon.
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
